           -------
           decfunc : function
               The decorator function that modifies the __doc__ attribute
               of its argument.
       
           Examples
           --------
           In the following, the docstring for Bar.func created using the
           docstring of `Foo.func`.
       
           >>> class Foo:
           ...     def func(self):
           ...         '''Do something useful.'''
           ...         return
           ...
           >>> class Bar(Foo):
           ...     @inherit_docstring_from(Foo)
           ...     def func(self):
           ...         '''%(super)s
           ...         Do it fast.
           ...         '''
           ...         return
           ...
